00:08.993 --> 00:12.223
"She has a total of 150 wooden boards

00:12.223 --> 00:14.853
and 330 nails.

00:14.853 --> 00:17.045
"The following inequality
represents the number

00:17.045 --> 00:19.589
"of tables, T, and chairs, C,

00:19.589 --> 00:23.246
"she can make with 150 wooden boards."

00:23.246 --> 00:26.566
So we can see the 150 wooden
boards right over here

00:26.566 --> 00:30.919
and it looks like she uses 17
wooden boards for each table

00:30.919 --> 00:34.467
so the total amount of
boards from the tables are

00:34.467 --> 00:37.428
to make the tables is 17 T.

00:37.428 --> 00:41.352
And it looks like she
uses six wooden boards

00:41.352 --> 00:43.348
for each chair and that's why you take

00:43.348 --> 00:45.368
six per chair times the number of chairs.

00:45.368 --> 00:47.110
This is the total number of wooden boards

00:47.110 --> 00:48.468
