00:48.468 --> 00:49.373
And you add them together.

00:49.373 --> 00:50.987
It can't be anymore than 150.

00:50.987 --> 00:53.634
She only has, I guess 150 wooden boards.

00:53.634 --> 00:56.193
"Additionally, the following
inequality represents

00:56.193 --> 00:57.593
"the number of tables and chairs

00:57.593 --> 01:00.170
"she can make with 330 nails."

01:00.170 --> 01:03.769
So once again, she has
the maximum of 330 nails.

01:03.769 --> 01:06.404
It looks like she needs 34 nails per table

01:06.404 --> 01:09.718
because the total nails from the tables is

01:09.718 --> 01:13.129
34 nails per table times
the number of tables.

01:13.129 --> 01:16.329
And then it looks like she needs 27 nails.

01:16.329 --> 01:20.869
It looks like she needs 27 nails per chair

01:20.869 --> 01:22.563
because the total nails that she uses

01:22.563 --> 01:25.180
