are 27 nails per chair

01:25.180 --> 01:27.205
times the number of chairs.

01:27.205 --> 01:28.714
"Does Fleur have enough boards

01:28.714 --> 01:31.755
"and nails to make three tables,

01:31.755 --> 01:33.695
"to make three,

01:34.135 --> 01:38.175
"to make three tables and nine chairs?

01:38.175 --> 01:40.253
"And nine chairs?"

01:40.253 --> 01:43.167
Let's see, let's look
at the number of boards.

01:43.167 --> 01:45.013
To make three tables and nine chairs,

01:45.013 --> 01:48.414
she's going to use 17 times T.

01:48.414 --> 01:49.796
In this case, it's three.

01:49.796 --> 01:54.796
Shes' going to use 17 times
three boards for the tables

01:54.950 --> 01:57.713
and then she is going to use,

01:57.713 --> 01:59.048
she is going to use

01:59.048 --> 02:02.914
six times the number of chairs.

02:02.914 --> 02:04.551
So six times nine chairs.

02:04.551 --> 02:07.047
Six boards per chair times nine chairs.

02:07.047 --> 02:08.614
So six times nine is the number of boards

02:08.614 --> 02:10.228
